    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0764" n="1598" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/111</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-30T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 30, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1426. Your January 22, 8 p.m. The attitude you adopted in respect of Swiss
                    negotiations with England for tonnage is approved. Under provisional agreement
                    just signed with Holland<anchor n="3" xml:id="d636-f1"/> a limited <pb
                        facs="0765" n="1599" xml:id="pg1599"/> amount of shipping will temporarily
                    be made available to transport grain to Switzerland but it is not desired that
                    you relax your efforts to induce Switzerland to meet England’s views so as to
                    facilitate procuring ships for Swiss use not only now but in the future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d636-f1" n="3" xml:id="d636-f1-content">
                <p>See note No. 648, Jan. 25, from the Netherland Minister, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1392">p. 1392</ref>.</p>
            </note>
